experimental_designs_or_analyses.value:
The general experimental design makes sense, although I believe the two baselines mentioned before are key to validate the impact of the proposed system. Besides that, It is not clear how challenging the presented setup is. The experiments are conducted in five healthy patients, in a stable walk of 1 m/s. The problem presents a state-space of 5 dimensions and action-space of 4 dimensions. Thus: 

1) It is unclear if the locomotion gaits from these five patients would indeed require a meaningful adaptation (in other words, how different should we expect their locomotion patterns to be?);

2) The state/action spaces are comparable to small benchmarks in RL; while I understand the major challenge comes from the lack of dynamics model and limited data, the presence of expert demonstrations also considerably mitigates that and provides a good base policy for downstream RL.

